tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212257Z -- The valve hold schedule (item 29)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212358Z   ok   a price spread earns a hold schedule
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212514Z   ok   and the schedule is fully resolved -- real temperatures, no sentinels
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212643Z   ok   it holds the valve down between charging and the peak
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212760Z   ok   and it never asks for a house below the comfort floor
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8212884Z   ok   the null control: flat prices earn no schedule at all
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213011Z   ok   a valve the integration cannot command gets no schedule
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213123Z   ok   and neither does a tank too small to be a store
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213257Z   ok   no candidate is derived where prices are flat
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213460Z   ok   nor where the plan never charges
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213608Z   ok   a charging plan against a spread does derive one
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213719Z   ok   the peak itself is never held down
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8213868Z   ok   a held valve really does keep heat in the tank
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8214003Z   ok   and no schedule is byte-for-byte the configured target
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8214193Z   ok   charging a full tank at full power is refused by the physics
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8214348Z   ok   the tighten loop cuts the ceiling at the refusing steps
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8214486Z   ok   even free electricity cannot plan past the tank's ceiling
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8214594Z   ok   and the trajectory itself respects the cap
