tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8754914Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755083Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755231Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755352Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755468Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755708Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755846Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8755983Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756142Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756248Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756359Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756514Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756658Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756786Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8756944Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8757066Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.8757290Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
