tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105012Z   ok   the write timeout is bounded well inside one update cycle
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105241Z   ok   control for the test registry: a rejected write raises only for blocking=True, as in Home Assistant core
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105405Z   ok   a switch with no state is not written, is not a failed write, and is not claimed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105591Z   ok   …and an unload keeps the record of an owned switch that has no state
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105760Z   ok   an accepted ON that does not read back on is a failed write with no ownership
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9105929Z   ok   …and an unload OFF that does not read back off keeps the record
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9106222Z   ok   control for the test registry: a blocking call to an id with no state returns without raising and without reaching a handler, as in booted core
