tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9109467Z   ok   …and the ON goes out on the first cycle the mode allows hot water, with no solve between
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9109627Z   ok   a switch that was already on is left alone through a whole boost and after it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9109807Z   ok   an idle control install writes nothing, not even OFF
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9109958Z   ok   a failed write raises a non-persistent repair naming the switch
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9110138Z   ok   …the next cycle retries the ON, and its success clears the repair
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9110272Z   ok   a failed OFF at the close is retried on the next idle cycle, once
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9110466Z   ok   an OFF the switch ignored is re-sent while it still reads on, and stops once it reads off
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9110776Z   ok   an owned switch that goes unavailable is waited for, then turned OFF when it is back on
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9110991Z   ok   restart mid-boost: the next run turns off the switch the last one turned on
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9111176Z   ok   …and once it read off, the store no longer names it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9111400Z   ok   reload into observe mid-boost: the owned switch is turned OFF and never back ON
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9111666Z   ok   reload onto another switch mid-boost: the new switch ON, the old one OFF, in the same cycle
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9112009Z   ok   renamed switch: the old record is kept through the grace, then dropped with a persistent repair naming it, and nothing is written blind
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9112314Z   ok   …and the drop is in the store, so a restart does not resurrect the record
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9112690Z   ok   deleted switch, new one configured: a boost drives the new switch on and off while the old record waits out its grace
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9113021Z   ok   deleted switch with the option unset and observe chosen: the record is dropped with its repair
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9113287Z   ok   switch unset while it reads on: OFF is sent to the recorded id and the record ends
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9113483Z   ok   a switch that loads after the optimizer at startup is still turned off, with no repair
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9113672Z   ok   unload turns off the switch the integration owns and, the OFF having landed, forgets it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T08:49:53.9113898Z   ok   …so a program the user starts while it is unloaded is left on at the next setup
